  "title": "Trung sisters' rebellion against Han rule",
  "summary": "In AD 40 the sisters Trung Trac and Trung Nhi led a rising against Han rule in the Red River region of northern Vietnam, over new taxes. Trac held court at Me Linh until a Han army sent by the emperor defeated them around AD 43. Accounts differ on whether the sisters drowned themselves or were beheaded.",
